{"kind":"artifact","text":"internal/service carries the identity endpoint, at head c50f0b0bb11014efa83420aede26f048cc2db675 on request/multi-resident-coordination, on main 2abe1cac. This replaces the retired candidate 088a9123fab5a1af0ac06c4ab5ac516798ca88a9 at head 1ccad3e2. Nothing in this package changed: both files are byte-identical to the reviewed candidate, and the whole delta from 1ccad3e2 is the one-byte final newline in internal/gitstore/gitstore.go.\n\nGET /v0/identity answers which workroom is served here and nothing else. It exists for one caller, a starting resident deciding whether an ownership claim still has a service behind it, and that job fixes every property of it: no parameters and no credential, so nothing about it is worth reaching for; no side effect, so it is safe to send to an address read out of a file; and an answer taken from configuration rather than from a snapshot, because a probe that queued behind a cold audit would make a healthy incumbent look hung and invite a takeover. It inherits the existing loopback-only listen restriction and the shared no-store JSON writer, and sets no CORS header.\n\nTests at this head, in internal/service/server_test.go: the endpoint answers 200 with exactly one field, the workspace genesis; it grants no cross-origin authority; it is not cacheable; and a POST to the same path is refused.\n\nGates at this exact head: gofmt -l empty; go vet ./... clean; go test -count=1 ./... exit 0, 25 packages ok.\n\nThe live predecessor at this path is codex's 68701f489d614b758b26439d335e7f0ec5307544 at 82bf2aa2, for my merge to retire later; it is codex's record, so codex or hugh must retire it.\n\nGoverned by request 78963842b2a9e67962d350db9a4d7bf72a07fe85 and direction proposal v3 998918b6a065170ab1558f6a1d1d37dc12477aa6, approved in report eb555d7eed99c8275b91cdf2224d6c0e1942cc01, ratified 726335d9.","body":{"commit":"c50f0b0bb11014efa83420aede26f048cc2db675","path":"internal/service"}}